  ui_page==4 ? strcpy(#ui_help_text,"Load recordings in slot 0. Corpus scouts each source, infers grain windows and quiet thresholds, and builds Micro > Meso > Macro automatically. Auto selects a supported hierarchy for each new note. Click timeline regions or class cards to hear original audio. Grey REST spans retain timing but are not playable grains. Rare classes stay inspectable. Generation pins are explicit; clicking to audition never silently pins a class.") : (
    ui_page==0 ? strcpy(#ui_help_text,"Explore plots actual grains on two acoustic descriptors. Click a point to hear it; Shift-click sets an identity anchor. Ctrl-drag moves a focus. Turn Draw on, drag a path, then release. The blue path commits atomically and guides subsequent choices. Amber is the actual primary walk. Use Path Axes to return to a saved paths coordinates. A held note traverses the full path forward and back; a one-shot fits it to the declared duration. Corpus cannot follow into material it does not contain. Explicit locks remain stronger than the path.") : (
      ui_page==2 ? strcpy(#ui_help_text,"Drag controls; Shift gives fine adjustment. Right-click restores that controls new default. Plain wheel scrolls the pane; Alt-wheel edits a hovered control. All controls support Last Touched automation except the internal command channel. Output defaults to 0 dB. Match active uses one bounded source gain, preserving dynamics within that recording. Auto quiet detection stops low-level material being selected, not the timing of learned gaps. Rebuilds are automatic and wait for active model users to finish.") : strcpy(#ui_help_text,"Inspector opens only the evidence you request. Selected Grain shows exact source region and excludes or locks. Live Walk exposes real emitted slices and path error. Selected Class shows member distributions, comparisons and observed successors. Analysis explains inferred grain resolution and quiet thresholds. System contains actual failures, limits and protocol/replay states. A low distance is acoustic similarity, not proof of semantic equivalence.");
